ernationally. It offers end-to-end logistics for production of alkylate for refineries mining, water treatment, and industrial applications. The company was formerly known as PQ Group Holdings Inc. and changed its name to Ecovyst Inc. in August 2021. Ecovyst Inc. was founded in 1831 and is headquartered in Wayne, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kurt J. Bitting | CEO & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 617 people. Revenue per employee of $1.2M ranks in the top quartile among Basic Materials peers, with revenue falling 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $113K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $16K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Ecovyst Inc. is a small-cap basic materials business with a $1.2B market cap on $724M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -4% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 26%.","The business throws off $70M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 1.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 58/100): structural revenue/margin decline; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Environmental remediation liability \u2014 tightening regulations on emissions, tailings, and water use create open-ended balance-sheet risk that grows with each legislative cycle.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Ecovyst (ECVT) Lifted Its 2026 Outlook, Is The Stock Cheap Or Pricey?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/materials/nyse-ecvt/ecovyst/news/ecovyst-ecvt-lifted-its-2026-outlook-is-the-stock-cheap-or-p","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794536446.023,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.93,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Reviewing Kuraray (OTCMKTS:KURRY) & Ecovyst (NYSE:ECVT)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/reviewing-kuraray-otcmktskurry-ecovyst-nyseecvt.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794399319.0,"orig